    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get what you're saying about the balance, but it feels like the \"multilateral\" approach hasn't really worked for a lot of people. like, for years it felt like the WTO just allowed countries to undercut everyone else with subsidies and unfair stuff while local workers lost everything. when people demand more sovereignty now, isn't it just a logical response to a system that stopped working for them? it almost seems like the \"globalist\" way is fundamentally broken at this point.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
